From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] egui-winit: the Amiga keys are command keys on AROS

Crate: egui-winit 0.37.0 from storytold/egui 6d518fc799681571963842f95b55a6b68431b15a,
  manifest made standalone by scripts/ea.py.
Date: 2026-10-28 (rebased from the egui-winit 0.36.2 series of 2026-10-19)
Problem: the AROS winit backend reports the left and right Amiga keys as
  Super. Outside macOS egui-winit takes `command` from Ctrl only and drops
  Super, so Amiga+C, Amiga+X, Amiga+V and every other Amiga shortcut do
  nothing in egui programs; on AROS these are the usual command keys (the
  shells of the PhotoCraft, WordCraft and PdfCraft AROS ports treat them so).
Rationale: on AROS `command` is Ctrl or an Amiga key; `ctrl` stays Ctrl, so
  programs that ask for Ctrl specifically are unchanged.
Scope: one expression.
Upstream-status: candidate for the AROS contrib crate store (not submitted).
Prerequisites: 0001-aros-system-clipboard.patch.
Verification: see the egui-aros build records (branch egui-0.37).
Rebase: in 0.37 the platform test is Context::os().is_mac(); the AROS
  branch is added after it, unchanged.
Removal: when the AROS crate store carries an equivalent change.
---
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 8e7315a..5431e37 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -2380,7 +2380,14 @@ impl State {
                 // `Context::set_os()` and `egui::os::OperatingSystem::from_user_agent()`).
                 let is_mac = self.egui_ctx.os().is_mac();
                 self.modifiers.mac_cmd = is_mac && super_;
-                self.modifiers.command = if is_mac { super_ } else { ctrl };
+                self.modifiers.command = if is_mac {
+                    super_
+                } else if cfg!(target_os = "aros") {
+                    // The Amiga keys (winit's Super) are AROS's command keys: Amiga+C copies.
+                    ctrl || super_
+                } else {
+                    ctrl
+                };
 
                 self.egui_input
                     .events
